id: pm-csv-rioq
title: "Correct a wrong shebang claim in the attestation launcher, and bring the canonical auditor up to date"
description: "Two problems, and the second explains the first.\n\nThe launcher docstring said the auditor 'treats any file whose first two bytes are a shebang as executable shell'. Reproduced against the auditor this repository now consumes, that is false: a shebang says a file executes, it does not say it executes AS shell, so only a shebang naming a shell interpreter makes the body shell input. Written into a throwaway git repository and run through verify(): #!/bin/bash and #!/usr/bin/env sh report the file by name; #!/usr/bin/env node and no shebang do not.\n\nThe claim was TRUE for pm-ops 2026.9.5, which this repository was still pinned to - two releases behind the canonical auditor, and therefore missing every fail-open construction closed since. Bumping to ^2026.9.7 is what makes the corrected claim correct, which is why the two changes belong together rather than as a docstring tidy.\n\nThe same wrong sentence is in all seven repositories carrying this launcher; it was propagated by copying the reference file, so the error travelled with the text. Corrected in the six sibling convergence branches at the same time.\n\nAlso re-exports auditPublishAttestation and verify by reference. The launcher previously exported only runIfMain, so the fleet's bypass-corpus harness read this repository as broken rather than as converged, and no test asserted that what the launcher exposes IS the package's function rather than a wrapper."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[2]: attestation,security
